// How an area loads (crates/base/src/areas.rs): its spawners run over
// several frames instead of all in one, so loading New York doesn't freeze
// the game for most of a second. Each frame the first spawner always runs,
// then more while there's budget left. The colliders of an area someone is
// standing in (they teleported there) all come at once, so nobody falls
// through. Edit and save: the game picks it up.
(
    // Milliseconds a frame may spend loading an area you're walking up to
    // (or a friend is in): keep it small, you're playing.
    walk_ms: 4.0,
    // The same for the area you're standing in while it loads (the loading
    // curtain is up): bigger, so it's done sooner.
    covered_ms: 40.0,
)
